-- Repro: BG body uses COPY on a captured outer-scope value. The
-- CaptureStrategy.classify path returns FreshHeapCopy for this case
-- (intent: fresh heap-copy at ctx-init time so the fiber owns its
-- own copy and the outer cleanup is independent), but FreshHeapCopy's
-- marker_plan ([:alloc_mark, ctx_init_name, alloc_sym], [:cleanup,
-- ctx_init_name, alloc_sym]) is computed and never emitted. Worse,
-- the `COPY x` expression INSIDE the BG body fails to lower at all:
--
--   MIREmitter: unknown node type Array (RuntimeError)
--   from src/mir/mir_emitter.rb:149
--
-- So FreshHeapCopy is doubly dead: the strategy is classified
-- correctly but neither the marker emission nor the body-side COPY
-- lowering is wired. Any user reaching this path either gets the
-- crash above (lowering failure) or, hypothetically once the
-- lowering crash is fixed, a UAF (heap copy not actually performed).
--
-- Fix path:
-- 1. lower_bg_block (or a body-statement lowering hook) handles
--    COPY of a captured @list: emit the deep-copy at ctx-init time
--    via FreshHeapCopy.marker_plan. Body becomes a read of the
--    pre-copied ctx field.
-- 2. The MIRChecker verifies the AllocMark/Cleanup pair from
--    marker_plan via INV-1/INV-2.
--
-- Until then this test crashes the lowering. Re-enable when COPY of
-- captured @list (or struct) inside a BG body lowers and runs
-- correctly.

FN main() RETURNS Void ->
    items: Int64[]@list = [];
    items.append(10_i64);
    items.append(20_i64);
    items.append(30_i64);
    p: ~Int64 = BG {
        snapshot = COPY items;
        snapshot[0_i64] + snapshot[1_i64] + snapshot[2_i64];
    };
    r = NEXT p;
    ASSERT r == 60_i64, "BG body COPY of captured @list snapshots correctly";
END
